 need it. The next player has pungs of W3 and W5, so maybe they don't need W4. So discarding W4 might be safer. \n\nSo the best action is Play W4.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The best move is to discard W4 to avoid giving others a chance to complete their melds and to keep the potential for forming a T5-T6-T7 chow.\nReason: Discarding W4 reduces the risk of aiding opponents, as the previous player already has a pung of W4. Keeping T5 and T7 allows for the possibility of completing a chow with T6 if drawn. Other tiles like W2 or T5 are less critical for immediate threats.\nAnswer: Play W4"}
